:'''NOTE:''' ''Classifications should only be applied on [[Empire of Cats|Revival of Bahamut-Cat]]'s [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] and beyond.''
'''Classification''' is an '''''unofficial''''' method that assigns [[Cat Units]] to a ''Class'' and defines their general role in the game.

[[File:135 4.png|thumb|360px|[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] is undoubtedly a Super-Backliner, and since his [[Freeze]] on [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] & [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] is about as impressive as his long attack range, he is also a Crowd-Controller. Additionally, he possesses a reliable and powerful [[Wave Attack]], solidifying him as a Waver on top of the above. ]]

__TOC__
Classification is highly dependent on interpreting units' stats, as relatively stronger traits will be preferred in order to obtain a fair judgement.

Some Cat Units fit comfortably into '''2''' classes, such as Ultima Galaxy Cosmo with the "Super-Backliner" and "Crowd-Controller" classes. However, most units only fit into one standard based on their range.

Different forms may also change a unit's class entirely. For example, [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Lord Gao]] is a unit with high range and remarkable stats, which could be given a wider phrase like "attacker." Despite his range and notable stats, Gao fits more into the Backliner class; whereas [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Baby Gao]] has lower range and weaker stats, but has a much shorter cooldown, requiring a reclassification into Midranger.

The greatest example of a Classification change can be seen from the [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Tales of the Nekoluga]] Gacha event: its Ubers and Legend Rare are all completely unusable before being upgraded into their Evolved Form, where most become Backliners or Super-Backliners.

Note that classes are mostly irrelevant until the third [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]] of Empire of Cats, where enemies start to become threats. In [[Empire of Cats]], enemies are so weak that most cats can perform any role, and access to cats with some classes is limited anyway. The first stage in the game where classes are applicable is Empire of Cats Chapter 3's Moon, where the [[Teacher Bun Bun|first threatening enemy]] is seen.

Due to there being a complete revamp of Classifications, it is recommended and supported for you to help us re-classify our Cats. The page most relevant to this is the [[Cat Release Order]], where you can observe all Cat Units, the majority of whom have not been reclassified yet.

==Range Classifications==
A unit has exactly one range classification, although different forms of the unit may have different classifications (such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]).

'''[[:Category:Melee-class Cats|Melee]]''' (1-249 range): e.g. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hip Hop Cat]], [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]], etc.<br>
'''[[:Category:Midranger-class Cats|Midranger]]''' (250-399 range): e.g. [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Maeda Keiji]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Figure Skating Cats]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]], etc.<br>
'''[[:Category:Backliner-class Cats|Backliner]]''' (400-499 range): e.g. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Baby Mola (Super Rare Cat)|Baby Mola]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]], etc.<br>
'''[[:Category:Super-Backliner-class Cats|Super-Backliner]]''' (500+ range): e.g. [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]], [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Nerd Cat]], etc.

==Main Role Classifications==
You can list multiple of these if the unit fits multiple roles. If a unit fits none of these roles (e.g., [[Thief Cat (Rare Cat)|Thief Cat]], who is not a nuker, rusher, tanker, waver, etc.) then leave it with only the range classification.

[[File:Windy Type a Attack Animation.gif|thumb|140px|[[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Windy, type α]] has very high damage against Floating enemies, and thus is able to "nuke" [[Teacher Bun Bun]].]]

'''[[:Category:Nuker-class Cats|Nukers]]''' typically have a slowish attack rate, and they always have extreme damage per hit. They often have a damage-boosting ability against one or more traits. Examples include:
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hip Hop Cat]]
*[[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]]...
{{Clear}}

'''[[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]]''' are extremely fast units, typically with shorter-than-average cooldowns, long backswings, high speed, and short/mid range. They often have high damage per hit and are able to do lots of damage quickly. Examples include:
*[[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]]
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]]...

[[File:Kai Type u Attack Animation.gif|thumb|140px|[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Kai, type μ]] has extremely high health and attack power, and can even "tank" hits from non-Floating enemies rather well.]]

'''[[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|Tankers]]''' are units who have extremely high HP and durability. They are used for taking hits from enemies without being knocked back, typically on stages where meatshields fall short. They often have a health-boosting ability against one or more traits and many of them have great attack power at a short range. Examples include:
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Dogumaru]]
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Curling Cat]]
*[[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sushi Cat]]...

:'' Although Tankers tend to have melee range, some of them (such as [[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|King Gamereon]]), have Midranger or even Backliner range. These units are often referred to as Ranged Tanks; they tend to have longer cooldowns than other tanks and can synergize better with meatshields.''
{{Clear}}

'''[[:Category:Sniper-class Cats|Snipers]]''' are units whose primary role is to kill backline enemies. They may use piercing attacks which can reach backlines protected by shorter ranged enemies. Or, they may simply stand further back than any enemy attack can reach, safely chipping away at the backline. Applies to many [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] and [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attack]] units. Examples include:
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Nerd Cat]]
*[[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Little Leaguer Cat]]
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Elder Beast Naala]]...

[[File:Manic Macho Legs Attack Animation.gif|thumb|140px|[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]]' wave is able to clear out the peons spawning from the base.]]

'''[[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wavers]]''' are units with the [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attack]] or [[:Category:Mini-Wave Cats|Mini-Wave]] ability. Most are also Snipers, but there are a few exceptions. The wave ability needs to be a major aspect of the unit's use for it to qualify as a Waver, so units with a low wave chance like [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan Cat]] are not considered Wavers. Examples include:
*[[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]]
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]]
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]...
{{Clear}}

[[File:Crowdcontrol.png|thumb|140px|[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]]'s guaranteed [[Weaken]] & [[Surge Attack|Surge]] can shut down almost any non-[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy, like a true Crowd-Controller.]]

'''[[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Controllers]]''' are units that are mainly used to [[Knockback|knockback]] enemies or inflict status effects (like [[Slow]], [[Freeze]], [[Weaken]], or [[Curse]]). Examples include:
*[[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]]
*[[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Onmyoji Cat]]
*[[Bodhisattva Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bodhisattva Cat]]...
{{Clear}}

[[File:Critical hit.png|thumb|140px|[[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] won't do much other than hurting Metals with [[Critical Hit]]s.]]

'''[[:Category:Critter-class Cats|Critters]]''' are units that have a reliable Critical ability. Examples include:
*[[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]]
*[[Backhoe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Backhoe Cat]]
*[[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]]...
{{Clear}}

[[File:001 3.png|thumb|140px|[[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] is a textbook example of a Meatshield, with low cost, low recharge time, and very high health.]]

'''[[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|Meatshields]]''' are units with a very low cost and minimal recharge time, even more preferably with the [[Survive]] ability and/or high health. Examples include:
*[[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]]
*[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]]
*[[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Pogo Cat]]...
{{Clear}}

==Miscellaneous Role Classifications==
[[File:377 1.png|thumb|140px|[[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fencer Cat]] can serve as an attacker, but is mainly used for his guaranteed chance to break Barriers.]]

'''[[:Category:Breaker-class Cats|Breakers]]''' are a small group of units that are mainly used for their ability to reliably destroy [[Barrier]]s or [[Shield]]s. Examples include:
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]]
*[[Furiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Furilan Pasalan]]
*[[Skirt Cat (Special Cat)|Loincloth Cat]]...
{{Clear}}

[[File:109 3.png|thumb|140px|[[Madam Bride (Rare Cat)|Madam the Savannah]] is pretty useless in battle, but is in several great Combos.]]

'''[[:Category:Combo Slave-class Cats|Combo Slaves]]''' are units that serve little to no purpose outside of [[Cat Combo]]s, where they can be used to great effect with other units. Examples include:
*[[Cat Boy (Special Cat)|Cat Boy]]
*[[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Killer Cat]]
*[[Rich Cat III (Super Rare Cat)|Rich Cat Sr.]]...
{{Clear}}

[[File:142 2.png|thumb|140px|[[Tutorial Cat (Special Cat)|Behind Tutorial]] has bad stats and is not in any Combos, so it only serves to increase the player's [[User Rank]].]]

'''[[:Category:User Rank Dump-class Cats|User Rank Dumps]]''' are nearly useless cats, with no meaningful Combos, very low stats or terrible performance in general. They are only ever used for boosting [[User Rank]] or as sacrifices in the [[Underground Labyrinth]]. As long as a unit can be upgraded, it classifies for User Rank Dump. These units often come from older collaboration events. Examples include:
*[[Clone Elle (Special Cat)|Clone Elle]]
*[[Swordsman (Rare Cat)|Swordsman]]
*[[Nubobo (Special Cat)|Nubobo]]...
{{Clear}}

==Official Classifications==
Although classifications are not used directly in [[The Battle Cats]], [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]] has occasionally given units their own official classification outside of the game itself.

In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou#Roles|YuruGeGe]], all allied units had '''roles''' (ロール ''rōru'') that could be used as criteria in the filter, making it easier to find units of specific classifications. Some units had multiple roles or even changed role as they evolved, such as [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A4%CC%A4%EA%A4%AB%A4%D9 Nurikabe], whose Normal and Evolved Forms had both Attacker and Tank roles, while his [[True Form]], Nuristal, was purely a Tank, trading most of his attack power, health, cost-efficiency and recharge speed for the Metal ability. See the YuruGeGe article for the list of roles.

During the [[PONOS Campaigns/Nyawards|Nyawards campaign]], players could vote for their favorite of five nominees from five different categories of units, including [[True Form]], Special Achievement, and three classifications. The classifications and nominees were:

*'''Defender''': [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sushi Cat]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]], [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]]
*'''Attacker''': [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hip Hop Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Mer-Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]
*'''Debuffer''': [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Apple Cat]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop Cat]], [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]], [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Gardener Cat]]

